~ _play_confrontation
Narrator: The trial chamber empties until only one reflection remains. It has Kaelen's face, Kaelen's posture, and none of Kaelen's exhaustion.
Mirror Kaelen: You passed the easy part. You admitted you are dangerous. Now comes the harder question.
Kaelen: What do I do with that?
Mirror Kaelen: No. Who gets to stop you when you are sure you are right?
Mirror Kaelen: You rejected obedience. Good. But defiance can become vanity if nobody can correct it.
Mirror Kaelen: You rejected the perfect rescue. Good. But urgency can become cruelty if nobody can slow it.
Mirror Kaelen: You rejected abandonment. Good. But commitment can become possession if nobody can name the difference.
Mirror Kaelen: You reached this place without naming the self you fear most. That is an answer too.
Kaelen: Then I need witnesses. Not followers. Not worshippers. People who can tell me no.
Elara: Finally. For the record, I have been ready to tell you no since the crater.
Seraphina: A commander who asks to be challenged may yet deserve command.
Lyra: I can do no. I am spectacular at no.
Mirror Kaelen: Then take the only useful gift a reflection can give.
Mirror Kaelen: Fragment Six is not a prize. It is a choir. Failed admin intelligences, abandoned by SOVEREIGN, repeating prayers made of broken permissions.
System: // FRAGMENT #6 TRAIL REFINED: CATHEDRAL_SERVER / CHOIR_OF_BROKEN_GODS
Mirror Kaelen: Go listen to the gods your code left behind.
Kaelen: And if they ask me to kneel?
Mirror Kaelen: Then remember what obedience sounded like in the plaza.

